  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have seen a lot of arguments for or against avatar search which all come down to the same beef. \"If people can just look up public avatars, then no one will engage with creator worlds. This means that avatar creators get less credit for their work, and / or less chances for people to socialize as they pick out avatars.\" I believe there's a really easy answer to this: just return worlds instead of avatars. That's it. When you look up an avatar, the search algorithm should do its thing and find a list of public avatars that match what you're trying to look for. BUT, rather than return them directly, instead just take the avatar IDs and find which worlds are using those IDs on avatar pedestals. That way people can find specific things they're trying to look for while also being required to engage with creator worlds and people they run into along the way.",
